\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Where this survey sits among published radio technosignature searches. Every limit plotted is a total-power limit for a signal narrower than the native channel of the experiment that set it, and those channels differ by 7{} orders of magnitude, from 2.79\,Hz{} to 31.2\,MHz, so a signal detectable by one programme need not be detectable by another at any power. \textbf  {(a)} Minimum detectable EIRP against distance on a common $5\sigma $ basis. This survey, the deepest window per star: blue circles where that window belongs to the carrier search and grey triangles for the 24{} stars whose only coverage is coarse-channel, which constrain an unresolved excess and not a drifting carrier (Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:quantities}); \emph  {filled}, that window's bare $5\sigma $ threshold, which carries no spectral-response correction and so stands on the same footing as the others; \emph  {open}, the same window at $\mathrm  {EIRP}_{90}$, the single-epoch trigger completeness of \S  \ref  {sec:pninetysel}, which does carry it and, like every limit here, excludes atmospheric decorrelation. Orange, \citet  {Enriquez2017}; aqua, \citet  {Margot2023}; violet, \citet  {Mason2025}; left-edge ticks, \citet  {Price2020}, each at its published limit rescaled to $5\sigma $ by the factor in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:litthresh}, with the published value as the hollow marker above it. \emph  {Compare the hollow markers with this survey's filled ones}, each programme at its own operating threshold: the rescaling puts thresholds on one arithmetic convention and not at a matched false-alarm probability (Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:falsealarm}). Grey dotted, EIRP $\propto d^{2}$ at constant received flux; green dashed, the 12\,m benchmark transmitter of \S  \ref  {sec:excludes}. No symbol carries a confirmation criterion, and completeness is measured only for this survey's open symbols. \textbf  {(b)} Native channel width against observing frequency for every searched window (filled, Class\nobreakspace  {}A; open, Class\nobreakspace  {}B), with the comparison programmes as horizontal segments at the widths of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:litthresh}.}}{3}{figure.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:context}{{1}{3}{Where this survey sits among published radio technosignature searches. Every limit plotted is a total-power limit for a signal narrower than the native channel of the experiment that set it, and those channels differ by \LtChanSpanDex {} orders of magnitude, from \LtChanNarrow {} to \LtChanWide , so a signal detectable by one programme need not be detectable by another at any power. \textbf {(a)} Minimum detectable EIRP against distance on a common $\LtCommonSnr \sigma $ basis. This survey, the deepest window per star: blue circles where that window belongs to the carrier search and grey triangles for the \NgNDecBOnly {} stars whose only coverage is coarse-channel, which constrain an unresolved excess and not a drifting carrier (Table~\ref {tab:quantities}); \emph {filled}, that window's bare $\LtCommonSnr \sigma $ threshold, which carries no spectral-response correction and so stands on the same footing as the others; \emph {open}, the same window at $\mathrm {EIRP}_{90}$, the single-epoch trigger completeness of \S \ref {sec:pninetysel}, which does carry it and, like every limit here, excludes atmospheric decorrelation. Orange, \citet {Enriquez2017}; aqua, \citet {Margot2023}; violet, \citet {Mason2025}; left-edge ticks, \citet {Price2020}, each at its published limit rescaled to $\LtCommonSnr \sigma $ by the factor in Table~\ref {tab:litthresh}, with the published value as the hollow marker above it. \emph {Compare the hollow markers with this survey's filled ones}, each programme at its own operating threshold: the rescaling puts thresholds on one arithmetic convention and not at a matched false-alarm probability (Appendix~\ref {app:falsealarm}). Grey dotted, EIRP $\propto d^{2}$ at constant received flux; green dashed, the \BenchDiam \,m benchmark transmitter of \S \ref {sec:excludes}. No symbol carries a confirmation criterion, and completeness is measured only for this survey's open symbols. \textbf {(b)} Native channel width against observing frequency for every searched window (filled, Class~A; open, Class~B), with the comparison programmes as horizontal segments at the widths of Table~\ref {tab:litthresh}}{figure.2.1}{}}
