\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B1}{\ignorespaces The $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pictoris positive control, in both directions. Both panels draw the same 52{} of the 56{} crossings, the remainder having no retained control ring. \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}The spatial screen: the stellar statistic against the maximum over that window's 512{} control positions. Filled symbols are the blocks in which the search recovers circumstellar carbon monoxide at $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pictoris, 9{} of them with the star above every control and one with the ring above it, block \texttt  {X7116f1\_X1785}, Band\nobreakspace  {}6, where the ring reaches 14.13{} against 9.68{} at the star (\S  \ref  {sec:bpicval}). \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}The same crossings by velocity offset from the nearest masked transition \emph  {in their own star's rest frame}, with the adopted $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ half-width marked: the 10{} $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pictoris carbon-monoxide crossings land 0.1--0.5\,km\,s$^{-1}$ from CO, while its 2{} unattributed crossings lie 3765--3870\,km\,s$^{-1}$ from the nearest transition the mask holds, CS($5{\to }4$). 39{} further crossings are grey, HD\nobreakspace  {}48370 marked.}}{32}{figure.B.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bpiccontrol}{{B1}{32}{The $\beta $~Pictoris positive control, in both directions. Both panels draw the same \BpicPanelNDrawn {} of the \NCross {} crossings, the remainder having no retained control ring. \emph {(a)}~The spatial screen: the stellar statistic against the maximum over that window's \NCtrl {} control positions. Filled symbols are the blocks in which the search recovers circumstellar carbon monoxide at $\beta $~Pictoris, \NStageOneBpicEb {} of them with the star above every control and one with the ring above it, block \texttt {\BpCtrlBlock }, Band~\BpCtrlBand , where the ring reaches \BpCtrlRingMax {} against \BpCtrlStar {} at the star (\S \ref {sec:bpicval}). \emph {(b)}~The same crossings by velocity offset from the nearest masked transition \emph {in their own star's rest frame}, with the adopted $\pm \MaskHalfKms $\,km\,s$^{-1}$ half-width marked: the \BpicPanelNCo {} $\beta $~Pictoris carbon-monoxide crossings land \BpicDvCoLo --\BpicDvCoHi \,km\,s$^{-1}$ from CO, while its \BpicPanelNCs {} unattributed crossings lie \BpicDvCsLo --\BpicDvCsHi \,km\,s$^{-1}$ from the nearest transition the mask holds, CS($5{\to }4$). \BpicPanelNOther {} further crossings are grey, HD~48370 marked}{figure.B.1}{}}
