\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {D3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The recurrence stage's positive controls, and the baseline each was recovered over.} The 13{} line-attributed crossings the criterion of \S  \ref  {sec:summary} recovers, toward 2{} stars: for each, the block whose own crossing satisfies it at the same stellar-frame frequency, that block's epoch, its separation from the discovery block and the statistic it reaches there. Block identifiers omit the constant \texttt  {A002\_} prefix and are printed as session and block, so the first field is the observing session: every recovering block belongs to a different session from its discovery block and lies more than 1{} day from it, as the criterion demands. $T$ is the statistic of that block's own crossing at that frequency, which is a maximum over every channel and drift of its window; $T_{\rm  rep}$ beside it is the single-cell reading at the cell the discovery predicts, taken in that same block through the frame correction, the start-of-block anchor and the carried drift, which is how the 33{} ledger exclusions are formed; and $T_{\rm  comb}$ is the same reading with all of that crossing's covering blocks combined, which is the quantity \S  \ref  {sec:etacrv} quotes. 11{} of the 13{} reach the trigger in the single block named here and 13{} with the blocks combined. $\Delta c$ is the cell's distance in channels from the brightest channel of that block's own search, a median 0.06{} of a channel over the readings that reach the trigger. On a resolved line that distance is not the line's position: the 10{} rows whose line is spread over as many as 69{} channels of their own window test the frame correction only to the width of that line -- the largest entry is 0.82\,km\,s$^{-1}$ in channels of 15.3\,kHz, inside a line 0.6{}--2.9\,km\,s$^{-1}$ wide -- and the registration of a single cell is tested by the 3{} rows of HD\nobreakspace  {}285968{} alone, whose line is confined to one channel and whose cells land within 0.06{} of one. $\dagger $\nobreakspace  {}marks a row involving the one window the archive delivers twice, once with the control annulus on this compact-array block's own antenna geometry and once on a nominal 12\,m beam (\S  \ref  {sec:summary}). The reading on the block's own geometry is the one published, 5.9557; the 12\,m annulus gives 6.1886{} for the same cell, 3.9{} per cent apart, 1.16{} per cent of that in the window noise and the rest in the recovered amplitude. The mark appears where that window supplies the reading and where it supplies the discovery the cell is predicted from; in the two rows where it supplies the reading, that is why the single-cell reading there stands above the window maximum beside it, the two being measurements of different products of one window. $\ddagger $\nobreakspace  {}marks a separation measured from an observing unit's stamp rather than from a block's own. Four{} of these crossings are present in blocks of their own observing unit as well, whose internal separations the archive does not record; the ledger file flags those rows in a column of its own.}}{38}{table.D.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:confirm}{{D3}{38}{\textbf {The recurrence stage's positive controls, and the baseline each was recovered over.} The \QcNCtl {} line-attributed crossings the criterion of \S \ref {sec:summary} recovers, toward \QcNStar {} stars: for each, the block whose own crossing satisfies it at the same stellar-frame frequency, that block's epoch, its separation from the discovery block and the statistic it reaches there. Block identifiers omit the constant \texttt {A002\_} prefix and are printed as session and block, so the first field is the observing session: every recovering block belongs to a different session from its discovery block and lies more than \EpSep {} day from it, as the criterion demands. $T$ is the statistic of that block's own crossing at that frequency, which is a maximum over every channel and drift of its window; $T_{\rm rep}$ beside it is the single-cell reading at the cell the discovery predicts, taken in that same block through the frame correction, the start-of-block anchor and the carried drift, which is how the \RcNExcl {} ledger exclusions are formed; and $T_{\rm comb}$ is the same reading with all of that crossing's covering blocks combined, which is the quantity \S \ref {sec:etacrv} quotes. \RgNCtlSingle {} of the \RgNCtl {} reach the trigger in the single block named here and \RgNCtlComb {} with the blocks combined. $\Delta c$ is the cell's distance in channels from the brightest channel of that block's own search, a median \RgCtlDchAbsMed {} of a channel over the readings that reach the trigger. On a resolved line that distance is not the line's position: the \RgRegNRes {} rows whose line is spread over as many as \RgResFwhmChMax {} channels of their own window test the frame correction only to the width of that line -- the largest entry is \RgOffMaxKms \,km\,s$^{-1}$ in channels of \RgOffMaxChanKHz \,kHz, inside a line \RgFwhmLoKms {}--\RgFwhmHiKms \,km\,s$^{-1}$ wide -- and the registration of a single cell is tested by the \RgRegNUnres {} rows of \RgRegStar {} alone, whose line is confined to one channel and whose cells land within \RgRegMaxCh {} of one. $\dagger $~marks a row involving the one window the archive delivers twice, once with the control annulus on this compact-array block's own antenna geometry and once on a nominal 12\,m beam (\S \ref {sec:summary}). The reading on the block's own geometry is the one published, \LrSuppPub ; the 12\,m annulus gives \LrSuppOwn {} for the same cell, \LrSuppPct {} per cent apart, \NbProvRmsPct {} per cent of that in the window noise and the rest in the recovered amplitude. The mark appears where that window supplies the reading and where it supplies the discovery the cell is predicted from; in the two rows where it supplies the reading, that is why the single-cell reading there stands above the window maximum beside it, the two being measurements of different products of one window. $\ddagger $~marks a separation measured from an observing unit's stamp rather than from a block's own. \QcNUnrecWord {} of these crossings are present in blocks of their own observing unit as well, whose internal separations the archive does not record; the ledger file flags those rows in a column of its own}{table.D.3}{}}
