\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {F1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Per-system sensitivity of the carrier search.} For each of the 61{} systems the fine-channel search covers, the $\mathrm  {EIRP}_{90}$ of its best window (Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:quantities}), with that window's own primary-beam, annual-parallax and smearing retentions applied, beside that window's centre frequency $\nu $ and native channel width $\Delta \nu $ and the system's merged coverage $\Delta \nu _{\rm  cov}$. Rows are ordered by the limit, and a gravitationally bound pair is one system under its primary's name. \textbf  {Every limit here is nominal in one respect: it excludes atmospheric decorrelation}, and \emph  {dec.} is the percentage by which that leaves it optimistic -- measured from the phase calibrator of its own execution block, starred where the delivery exposes no phase record and the figure is the median of the blocks matched to it in baseline length, and dashed for $\epsilon $\nobreakspace  {}Eri, the one system whose blocks offer neither (\S  \ref  {sec:pninetysel}). It is reported and not folded in; $\epsilon $\nobreakspace  {}Eri's window also omits the annual parallax and is optimistic by at most 9{} per cent on that account (Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:pbresp}). The last column records whether two execution blocks of different observing sessions cover a common frequency more than one day apart (d) or more than a year apart (yr), over the primary census together with the 166{} repeat blocks the recurrence test of \S  \ref  {sec:etacrv} reads, of which 42{} lie outside the census (\S  \ref  {sec:confirmability}). Both are lower bounds, since two blocks can be shown to be separated but never shown to be simultaneous. \textbf  {A dagger marks the 6{} systems whose own best window was one of the 49{} injected into, so that their completeness is measured}; the other 55{} limits are transferred from the class average and carry instead the dispersion observed between injected windows, $\times 0.80$ to $\times 1.58$, wider than the calibration interval of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:p90budget}.}}{40}{table.F.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:persys}{{F1}{40}{\textbf {Per-system sensitivity of the carrier search.} For each of the \NSysClassA {} systems the fine-channel search covers, the $\mathrm {EIRP}_{90}$ of its best window (Table~\ref {tab:quantities}), with that window's own primary-beam, annual-parallax and smearing retentions applied, beside that window's centre frequency $\nu $ and native channel width $\Delta \nu $ and the system's merged coverage $\Delta \nu _{\rm cov}$. Rows are ordered by the limit, and a gravitationally bound pair is one system under its primary's name. \textbf {Every limit here is nominal in one respect: it excludes atmospheric decorrelation}, and \emph {dec.} is the percentage by which that leaves it optimistic -- measured from the phase calibrator of its own execution block, starred where the delivery exposes no phase record and the figure is the median of the blocks matched to it in baseline length, and dashed for $\epsilon $~Eri, the one system whose blocks offer neither (\S \ref {sec:pninetysel}). It is reported and not folded in; $\epsilon $~Eri's window also omits the annual parallax and is optimistic by at most \BmEpsPxBoundPct {} per cent on that account (Appendix~\ref {app:pbresp}). The last column records whether two execution blocks of different observing sessions cover a common frequency more than one day apart (d) or more than a year apart (yr), over the primary census together with the \ZcNRecEB {} repeat blocks the recurrence test of \S \ref {sec:etacrv} reads, of which \ZcNRecEBOut {} lie outside the census (\S \ref {sec:confirmability}). Both are lower bounds, since two blocks can be shown to be separated but never shown to be simultaneous. \textbf {A dagger marks the \SmcNMeasSys {} systems whose own best window was one of the \SensNInj {} injected into, so that their completeness is measured}; the other \SmcNEstSys {} limits are transferred from the class average and carry instead the dispersion observed between injected windows, $\times \SmcDispLo $ to $\times \SmcDispHi $, wider than the calibration interval of Table~\ref {tab:p90budget}}{table.F.1}{}}
